SupraLINUX integrates the unchanged signed official Plasma 6.7.5 source.
Preserve the authenticated Ubuntu single binary, metadata, icons, translations
and documentation; BUILD_DOC stays enabled. Source declares no native CTest
suites. The native-test result is not-applicable, never an invented test PASS.

All direct Frameworks build dependencies are pinned to the reviewed eligible
29-node, 117-binary closure. Historical scope is preserved; actual reuse checks
bytes, source package, Debian version and architecture in the KVM lane.

Original Ubuntu preparation compiled the public Qt client and exercised the
installed menu editor on a closed owned bus and private Xvfb/XDG profile. The
same client bytes and original fixture run after APT upgrade. Actual operations
rename a private seed entry, create a submenu and application with exact Exec,
save menu/desktop/directory files, select through the public D-Bus API, capture
actual software pixels, close/reopen and edit the persisted entry. The original
seed remains byte-identical. The fixture explicitly uses ShowMenuBar=true and
waits for modal sycoca rebuilds on its bare Xvfb server. Input targets require
the explicit owned display, verified process PID and a mapped window. Metadata
BadWindow races are tolerated only for reads; invalid focus still fails through
cleanup. Whole owned groups and runtime are removed on both outcomes.

No launcher program runs. Full desktop/global shortcuts, default hidden-menu-bar
interaction, cutting/reordering and actual launch integration remain session QA.
No KDE source patch, Qt substitution or removed product function is introduced.
Local preparation is not candidate package certification or a package Attempt.
